WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.476
A half pipe is a U shape. A skater is low only between the two edges, and high outside them. A quadratic graph is the same: below the axis between two crossing points, above it outside them.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:29.469
A quadratic inequality has x squared in it, like three x squared minus eight x minus three is less than nought. The critical values are the x values where it equals nought. They are the boundaries.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:42.228
Which region do we want? For a U shape, less than nought means between the two roots. Greater than nought means outside them, written as two separate inequalities.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:51.566
This question type asks: find the set of values of x. Give one interval for inside, or two inequalities for outside.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:01:06.450
Step one: move every term to one side, so the other side is nought. Keep the x squared positive if you can. Collect carefully. This is where slips happen.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:20.003
Step two: solve the equals nought version, by factorising or the formula. These are the critical values. Step three: sketch the parabola through them. The sketch shows the region.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:31.068
Steps four and five: choose inside for less than nought, or two outside parts for greater than nought. The trap is joining outside parts into one inequality.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:44.689
January twenty twenty three. Find the set of values of x for which three x squared, minus eight x, minus three, is less than nought. Four marks.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:52.925
Step one: one side is already nought, and the x squared coefficient, three, is positive. So the graph is a U shape.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:02:08.513
Step two: solve three x squared minus eight x minus three equals nought. It factorises as three x plus one, times x minus three. So x is minus a third, or three. These are the critical values.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:21.065
Step three: sketch the U through minus a third and three. We want the expression to be less than nought. That is where the curve is below the axis, shaded here.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:30.968
Step four: choose the region. The curve is below the axis between the roots. So the answer is x between minus a third and three.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:43.298
A tempting wrong route is the outside region, x less than minus a third, or x greater than three. That is the answer to greater than nought. We need less than.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:54.861
Check. At x equals nought the value is minus three, less than nought, and nought is between the roots. At x equals four the value is thirteen, so it fails.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:03.678
So the set of values is x between minus a third and three. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:17.896
A common mistake is joining outside regions into one inequality. Three is less than x is less than minus a half is impossible. Write two inequalities with or.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:33.343
Now you try, from June twenty twenty five. Find the set of values of x for which ten x squared, plus seven x, is less than twelve. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:49.982
Move twelve across: ten x squared plus seven x minus twelve is less than nought. It factorises as two x plus three, times five x minus four. The critical values are minus three halves and four fifths.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:59.837
The coefficient is positive, so the graph is a U. Less than nought means below the axis, between the roots: x between minus three halves and four fifths.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:10.300
The common wrong answer factorises without moving the twelve across, giving x less than twelve. That is wrong. One side must be nought first.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:16.565
Remember: one side zero, find the critical values, sketch the U, choose the region, and write the set.
